[{:adr/id "2607163000"
  :adr/title "cloud-murakumo-market-intel: full SEC EDGAR backfill (28->5200 companies), staleness/negative-revenue fixes, raw-archive scale limit discovered"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-16"
  :db/id -1
  :adr/related ["2607150200-cloud-murakumo-market-intel-sec-edgar-company-facts"
                "2607151950-etzhayyim-gov-sec-edgar-raw-xbrl-archive"]
  :adr/sanitize-gate-worked-as-designed-mi-full "first full run (8021 CIKs) correctly aborted with NO partial write when sane-entity? flagged 10 entities -- exactly the fail-loud-no-partial-write behavior designed in ADR-2607150200, not a failure of the pipeline"
  :adr/two-distinct-root-causes-mi-full "(A) 8 commodity trusts/ETFs (iShares Gold/Silver Trust, US Oil/Gas/Brent/Natural Gas Funds etc.) had their only-present revenue-tag-priority candidate report a stale value (verified live: iShares Gold Trust's us-gaap:Revenues latest entry is dated 2013-12-31, 13 years stale relative to this run; Assets tag similarly stale at 2014-12-31) -- pick-annual's cross-tag recency selection (the Apple stale-tag fix from ADR-2607150200) was working correctly, there was just no check for 'the best available candidate is itself too old to report as current'. (B) 2 real operating companies (Beneficient CIK0001775734, VIP Play Inc CIK0001832161) have genuinely CURRENT (2026-03-31 / 2025-06-30) negative revenue -- a real accounting outcome (contra-revenue/fair-value items), not a bug; the blanket revenue>=0 sanitize assumption was simply wrong."
  :adr/staleness-filter-fix-mi-full "pick-annual's selected candidate is discarded (field becomes nil, not a stale number reported as current) if its :end year is more than 5 years older than the current year. Portable-.cljc-no-wall-clock discipline preserved (mirrors market-analyst/policy.cljc's staleness-violation pattern) -- current year is supplied by JVM-only market-intel.ingest/now-year, never read inside feed.cljc itself. Applies uniformly to revenue/assets/net-income (iShares Gold Trust's Assets tag was ALSO stale, not just Revenues)."
  :adr/negative-revenue-fix-mi-full "non-negative-financials-ok?'s revenue-side check removed entirely (assets-side non-negative check kept -- negative assets is a true accounting invariant violation, unlike revenue). Real examples (Beneficient, VIP Play) documented as the justification, not a hypothetical."
  :adr/full-backfill-result-mi-full "8021 CIKs in roster, 5200 yielded a company entity (2821 had no us-gaap companyfacts document at all -- IFRS-only foreign private issuers/shells, real 404 not error), 0 HTTP errors, sanitize gate passed after the fix. Landed as PR (not auto-merge) per the 'first large batch gets human review' convention; merge commit caf9d49a43a6fae23b34f20fa8bc0a01d4cbb368."
  :adr/raw-archive-scale-discovery-mi-full "IMPORTANT COURSE CORRECTION: attempting the same full-backfill's raw JSON archival into etzhayyim/gov.sec.edgar produced an 11GB .git (large financial institutions have 8MB+ per-company XBRL history JSON; 6989 companies aggregate to ~11GB). ADR-2607151950's decision to use text2git (based on a 28-company/11.6KB sample) is now known to have been wrong at full scale -- text2git only routes BINARY files to annex/B2, so large JSON text still lands directly in git history, exactly the clone/pull bloat this workspace's large-binary-datalad policy exists to prevent. The 11GB commit was created LOCALLY ONLY, verified, and discarded WITHOUT ever being pushed -- gov.sec.edgar's main remains at its original 28 companies. Full-scale raw archival requires .gitattributes reconfigured to annex large text files by size (not just binary mimeencoding) AND the still-unresolved B2 special remote (ADR-2607151950's bucket-ownership/1Password-Master-key blocker) -- both explicit follow-ups, not attempted in this ADR."
  :adr/lesson-small-sample-extrapolation "explicit lesson for future scale judgments in this workspace: a 28-company (11.6KB) sample was not representative of full-scale (thousands of companies, some with megabytes of XBRL history each) data volume -- measure at representative scale, or at minimum sanity-check the largest known outliers, before concluding a dataset is 'too small for DataLad'."
